provider "aws" {
    region = "us-west-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "test" {
  bucket        = "metricbeat-test-bucket"
  force_destroy = true // Required for cleanup
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_metric" "test" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.test.id
  name   = "EntireBucket"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_object" "test" {
  key     = "someobject"
  bucket  = aws_s3_bucket.test.id
  content = "something"
}

responsePreview:
This Terraform configuration creates an AWS S3 bucket resource named `my_bucket` with `force_destroy = true` so it can be deleted even if it contains objects. Because AWS S3 bucket names cannot contain underscores and must be globally unique, the actual bucket name uses a valid `my-bucket-*` format with a random suffix. It also creates a bucket metric named `my_bucket_metric` that monitors the entire bucket, and uploads an object named `my_object` with a specific key and content.

